@startuml seq_flt_oil_temp_sensor
title SC-FLT-03 - Oil temperature sensor out of range: substitute 80 degC, mode Normal

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU
participant "Red LED\n(TCU board)" as LED

note over User, LED
Covers: SYS-SEN-003, SYS-SEN-004, SYS-FLT-005, SYS-FLT-008, SYS-HMI-001, SIM-CON-003, SG-04
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
Valid electrical range 200 .. 4800 mV (can_matrix section 4).
end note

note over TCU: control active, mode Normal, no other fault
User -> Console : force OilTempVoltage (open circuit 0 mV or short circuit 5000 mV) (SIM-CON-003)
Console -> Plant : sensor voltage forced
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Analog: OilTempVoltage = 0 mV (t0)
loop every 10 ms
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Analog: OilTempVoltage outside 200 .. 4800 mV
end
... outside 200 .. 4800 mV for longer than 100 ms ...
TCU -> TCU : t0 + 100 ms: oil temperature sensor fault (FaultBits 5, DTC P0710-1C) (SYS-SEN-004)
TCU -> TCU : substitute oil temperature 80 degC, stay in mode Normal (SYS-FLT-005)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: FaultLamp = ON, shift control continues
TCU -> LED : ON (SYS-HMI-001)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: Mode = 0 (Normal), FaultBits bit 5 = 1

User -> Console : remove the injection
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Analog: OilTempVoltage within 200 .. 4800 mV (t1)
... within 200 .. 4800 mV for 100 ms ...
TCU -> TCU : t1 + 100 ms: oil temperature sensor fault cleared,\nmeasured oil temperature used again (SYS-FLT-008, SYS-SEN-003)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: FaultLamp = OFF (no other fault requires it, SYS-HMI-001)
TCU -> LED : OFF
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: FaultBits bit 5 = 0

note over Plant, TCU: In limp-home the lamp stays ON after the recovery (SYS-FLT-001, SYS-HMI-001).
@enduml
